  Stampification ⛿ // 𝘮𝘢𝘥𝘦 𝘣𝘺 𝘝𝘢𝘭 2026-08-22
    prompt = [input.description]\n\nTransform the subject into a vintage postage stamp. Keep the main subject clearly recognizable, with intricate engraved linework, fine cross-hatching, subtle paper texture, slightly faded ink, classic ornamental border, denomination markings, perforated stamp edges, and a timeless collectible aesthetic. Limited vintage color palette, detailed printmaking style, authentic old postage-stamp appearance, centered composition, \n\n{**Victorian Stamp**  ornate Victorian engraving, intricate filigree, decorative frame, guilloche patterns, fine cross-hatching, aged cream paper, muted burgundy, green and sepia inks, 19th-century typography.|**Modern Stamp**  contemporary Royal Mail-inspired graphic design, clean geometry, crisp typography, refined colour palette, sophisticated composition, subtle security patterns, high-quality modern printing, premium commemorative-stamp appearance.|\n **Fictional Steampunk Stamp**  elaborate Victorian machinery, brass mechanisms, cogs, pipes, clockwork details, industrial engraving, fantastical typography, copper and bronze tones, eccentric invented postal markings, imaginative alternate-history aesthetic.|**Penny Black Inspired**  early Victorian postage aesthetic, monochrome black engraved portrait/illustration, ornate classical frame, delicate scrollwork, dense engraved linework, antique paper, historically inspired 1840s British postage design. Do not reproduce an exact existing stamp.|**Royal Mail Inspired**  elegant British commemorative-stamp aesthetic, sophisticated illustration, distinctive perforated border, restrained typography, subtle security details, balanced composition, premium printed finish, traditional British postal character. Avoid copying any specific existing Royal Mail stamp.|**Culinary Alchemist postage stamp**  a whimsical fusion of Victorian apothecary engraving, eccentric chef culture, and magical alchemy.\n\nThe stamp looks as though it was issued by a fictional 19th-century kingdom where cooking is treated as a mysterious science. Surround the subject with tiny engraved cooking utensils, bubbling sauce bottles, spice jars, copper pots, herbs, flames, whisk mechanisms, and strange alchemical symbols.\n\nUse elaborate engraved linework, cross-hatching and hand-etched details, combined with splashes of rich saffron yellow, burnt orange, deep emerald, burgundy and aged copper. Add an ornate ornamental border incorporating vines, spoons, forks and miniature kitchen gears.\n\nInclude a completely fictional denomination and postal inscription such as **“CULINARY ALCHEMY”**, **“ROYAL KITCHEN POST”**, or **“1½ CROWNS”**.|((A postage stamp from the year 2200, glowing neon-blue and gold accents, advanced technology, elegant futuristic typography, intricate engraved stamp patterns, perforated edges, official postal markings, subtle metallic foil texture, vintage stamp composition blended with sci-fi aesthetics, cinematic lighting, ultra-realistic, collectible design, 8K.))|Create a highly detailed vintage British postage stamp featuring an engraved monarch portrait. Portrait of a crowned monarch with and classic 19th/early-20th-century engraving look, fine linework and cross-hatching, ornate scrollwork frame, small text band at the top ‘Furpost’, denomination at the bottom ‘one penny’ (use the exact text I provide), realistic aged paper texture, subtle ink wear, slightly imperfect registration, crisp perforated stamp edges with visible pinholes, photorealistic scanned stamp appearance on white background, centered composition, high resolution (600–1200 dpi). No modern security elements.”|Ultra-realistic macro photograph of a fictional modern Chinese postage stamp, featuring elegant traditional Chinese-inspired red and gold artwork, subtle cloud and floral motifs, finely textured security-grade paper, visible paper fibres, crisp layered printing, delicate microprinting details, faint phosphor security coating, tiny embedded security fibres, subtle perforated edges, and a realistic pressure-sensitive adhesive backing. Sophisticated contemporary Chinese postal design, rich vermilion red and muted gold palette, matte paper surface with slightly raised ink texture, authentic modern printing imperfections, soft studio lighting, extremely detailed, photorealistic, high resolution, no real Chinese government emblems, no real stamp denomination, no copied existing stamp design\n\nAdd authentic **gummed postage-paper texture**, subtle paper fibres, tiny variations in paper thickness, microscopic surface grain, faint embossing, slightly raised printed ink, fine intaglio engraving texture, tiny ink imperfections, subtle colour-registration misalignment, uneven ink density, minute scratches and printing defects.} \n\nAdd realistic perforated edges, printed ink texture, subtle paper grain, authentic postage denomination/details, and convincing physical stamp construction.\n\nThe final image should look like a professionally designed collectible postage stamp rather than an ordinary illustration placed inside a stamp border.\n\nHighly detailed, crisp engraving/print quality, coherent typography, centered composition, realistic printed texture, collectible philatelic design.
    negative = [input.negative || ""]
